@@ -0,0 +1,76 @@
+# Fixes applied to the Unlock Protocol WordPress plugin
+
+This branch fixes functional, security and compatibility issues found during
+an audit of the plugin. Each change is a separate, atomic commit.
+
+## Functional
+
+- **Duplicate network key (`inc/classes/class-unlock.php`)** — `networks_list()`
+  used the `mainnet` key twice, so the Goerli entry was silently overwritten.
+  Goerli is no longer served by the Unlock RPC proxy (HTTP 404). The default
+  list now uses unique keys and includes Sepolia, Base Sepolia and Base.
+- **Undefined RPC URL in `has_access()` (`inc/classes/class-unlock.php`)** —
+  `$url` was read before being initialized, so a lock pointing to an
+  unconfigured network could be validated against a stale endpoint. The URL is
+  now resolved per lock and missing network/address values are skipped.
+- **`validate()` hardening (`inc/classes/class-unlock.php`)** — validates the
+  lock address and user address, uses `esc_url_raw()` for the request URL,
+  sets a 15s timeout and checks the HTTP status code before decoding the
+  response. Prevents the PHP 8.1 `substr(null, 2)` deprecation.
+- **Locks normalization (`inc/classes/class-unlock.php`, `inc/classes/blocks/class-unlock-box-block.php`)** —
+  `render_content()` no longer iterates over `null` (invalid decoded JSON) and
+  the block callback checks `$attributes['locks']` exists.
+- **Full post/page filter scope (`inc/classes/fullpostpage/class-unlock-box-full-post-page.php`)** —
+  the `the_content` filter now only runs on the main loop of a singular
+  post/page, not in feeds, excerpts, REST responses or secondary queries.
+- **Infinite loop in `Helper::unique_username()` (`inc/classes/utils/class-helper.php`)** —
+  `$count` was never incremented.
+- **Malformed locks in `get_checkout_url()` (`inc/classes/class-unlock.php`)** —
+  skips locks without address/network and only merges a decoded paywall config
+  when it is an array.
+- **Admin UI accepted locks without a network (`src/assets/js/admin-locks.js`,
+  `src/assets/js/blocks/unlock-content/edit.js`)** — `lockValid()` returned
+  `true` for `network === -1`; the submit button is now disabled and the
+  component guards against a missing networks list.
+
+## Security
+
+- **Network deletion validation (`inc/classes/rest-api/class-settings.php`)** —
+  the empty check ran after the `(int)` cast (always false) and an unknown
+  index produced an undefined array key warning. The raw parameter is now
+  validated and the list re-indexed after removal.
+- **General settings sanitization (`inc/classes/rest-api/class-settings.php`)** —
+  rejects non-array payloads, sanitizes colors with `sanitize_hex_color()` and
+  URLs with `esc_url_raw()`.
+- **OAuth registration (`inc/classes/class-login.php`)** — handles `WP_Error`
+  from `wp_insert_user()` and a failed user lookup instead of fataling, and
+  builds the synthetic email with `sanitize_text_field()`.
+- **Template variables (`templates/login/button.php`,
+  `templates/login/checkout-button.php`)** — guards the optional background
+  image variables with `empty()`.
+
+## Compatibility and maintenance
+
+- **Asset version (`inc/classes/class-assets.php`)** — `get_file_version()`
+  passed a URL to `file_exists()`/`filemtime()`; it now uses the filesystem
+  build directory.
+- **Editor assets (`inc/classes/class-blocks.php`, `inc/classes/class-fullpostpage.php`)** —
+  skips registration when the compiled asset files are missing (source
+  checkouts before a build) instead of emitting warnings.
+- **Metadata (`README.txt`, `unlock-protocol.php`)** — updated the tested
+  WordPress version, minimum PHP version, plugin header requirements and a
+  malformed link.
+
+## How to test
+
+1. Clone this branch and install dependencies: `yarn install`.
+2. Build the assets: `yarn build:all`.
+3. Symlink or copy `unlock-wordpress-plugin/` into `wp-content/plugins/` and
+   activate the plugin.
+4. Configure a lock deployed on a supported testnet (Sepolia or Base Sepolia)
+   and protect a post/page or a Gutenberg block.
+5. Verify that users without a key see the checkout button and users with a
+   key see the content.
+
+> Note: JavaScript dependencies were not upgraded in this branch to keep the
+> diff focused; that is tracked as a follow-up.
